-- =======================================================================================
-- **ZERO checker errors, and the emitter refuses it by name.**
--
-- This probe exists to drive one case through `instrumente/zaehle-pflichten.py`'s lowering
-- classifier, and the case is the one the classifier's own criterion says cannot happen.
--
-- The criterion is two lines of prose above `_pruefe_fehler` (`zaehle-pflichten.py`:326-330):
--
--     `gabbro pruefe F` == 0 errors  ->  the language ACCEPTS the text and only the
--                                        generator is missing. Write the emitter arm and
--                                        the obligation is discharged. **PLUMBING.**
--
-- **Measured 2026-09-04, on this file:**
--
--     ./target/debug/gabbro pruefe  <this file>   ->  5 items, 0 errors, 0 hints
--     ./target/debug/gabbro emit    <this file>   ->  exit 1, and:
--       error: [C001] :65:5: no lowering: `queue` -- «B10»: `traverse` yields no value and
--       knows no `break`, so `by consuming` drains the WHOLE queue; that is a different
--       program
--
-- and through the classifier itself, as its own `sonde` (the probe handle it carries so a
-- case can be driven through without touching the tree):
--
--     zp.absenkungsklasse(sonde=("QSONDE", Path("q-sonde.gab")), locker=False)
--     ->  klempnerei (PLUMBING): ['QSONDE']      notation: ['F3']
--
-- **The classifier books it as PLUMBING.** It is not plumbing. `emit.rs`:8639 refuses
-- `Domaene::Schlange(_)` in an UNCONDITIONAL match arm, and the refusal text is the reason:
-- lowering it without an early exit computes something else. There is no arm being withheld.
--
-- > **This is the other half of `messung/AUDIT-K100-2026-09-04.md`.** That audit refuted the
-- > `> 0 errors` branch -- it reads a COUNT and never a REASON. This refutes the `== 0`
-- > branch, and by the same measure: *zero errors does not entail that only the generator is
-- > missing.* A criterion wrong in both directions is not a threshold that needs moving.
--
-- **Nothing here is chosen to provoke.** The construct is `F03`:185 in isolation --
-- `traverse … over queue … by consuming` -- and the surrounding declarations are the
-- smallest that let it parse and check. No name, no number and no clause is taken from
-- `messung/fragmente/F03.gab`; the point is that the construct ALONE carries the refusal,
-- so `F03`'s eighteen checker errors are not what stands between it and a Durchstich.
-- =======================================================================================

module probe::q {

const KAP : u32 = 32;

type TidQueue = {
    buf   : [u32; 32],
    head  : u32 in 0 ..< 32,
    tail  : u32 in 0 ..< 32,
    count : u32 in 0 .. 32,
};

table Halter count 4 {
    slot {
        wartende : TidQueue,
    }
}

impl fn leeren(e : ptr<normal, rw> Halter, k : index into Halter) -> u32
    effects { writes e.slots, consumes e.slots }
    costs   <= 100 ops
{
    let mut n : u32 = 0;
    traverse cand over queue e.slots[k].wartende by consuming
        touches consumes e.slots
    {
        n = cand;
    }
    return n;
}
}
